@startuml
title Viewing current dietary preferences
autonumber
participant "parser: Parser" as P
participant "view: Command lambda" as C
participant "settings: DietarySettings" as S
participant "profile: DietaryPreferences" as D
[-> P : parseCommand("view-diet")
activate P
P -> P : requireNoDietArguments(commandWord, arguments)
note over P : Extra arguments throw MishMashException with usage.
create C
P -> C : create lambda capturing shared settings
P -->[ : command
deactivate P
note over C, S : Settings may change between parsing and execution.
[-> C : execute(recipeBook)
activate C
C -> S : get()
S --> C : current profile
C -> D : describe()
D --> C : diet and sorted exclusion lists
C -->[ : three-line description
deactivate C
legend bottom
  The lambda is shown as a Command instance; it is not a named Java class.
  No recipe, plan, grocery, or preference mutation occurs.
  Dispatch helpers and string formatting internals are condensed.
endlegend
@enduml
